WEBVTT

00:00.726 --> 00:04.517
♪ It seems today that all you see ♪

00:04.518 --> 00:07.800
♪ Is violence in
movies and sex on TV ♪

00:07.801 --> 00:11.417
♪ But where are those good
old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.418 --> 00:14.432
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.433 --> 00:17.949
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.950 --> 00:21.104
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.105 --> 00:22.807
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.808 --> 00:24.214
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.215 --> 00:27.731
♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:30.896 --> 00:32.589
Hi there. It's me, Peter.

00:32.590 --> 00:35.367
You know, when it comes to
making dreams come alive,

00:35.368 --> 00:37.542
there used to be nothing
like the movies.

00:37.543 --> 00:39.119
So we thought it would be fun to ask

00:39.120 --> 00:42.536
a few visionary Hollywood
directors to create his...

00:42.537 --> 00:43.977
Let's be honest, his...

00:43.978 --> 00:47.058
Own unique version of the
same Family Guy story,

00:47.059 --> 00:48.559
"Peter Gets Fired."

00:48.560 --> 00:50.810
Of the countless
directors we contacted,

00:50.811 --> 00:53.087
three did not say no immediately,

00:53.088 --> 00:55.600
and I got a weird message
from Paul Verhoeven

00:55.601 --> 00:57.542
that I could not understand.

00:57.543 --> 00:59.452
Ah, Pieoter, habinsky Vermhoeven.

00:59.453 --> 01:01.462
Kibbensme comfurdle. Stupf.

01:01.463 --> 01:03.338
I've listened to that
over a hundred times now.

01:03.339 --> 01:04.577
I-I got nothin'.

01:04.578 --> 01:05.985
Anyway, here's our first director,

01:05.986 --> 01:07.815
Quentin Tarantino.

01:11.278 --> 01:13.520
♪ Hey, well, I'm the
friendly stranger ♪

01:13.521 --> 01:17.038
♪ In the black sedan, won't
you hop inside my car? ♪

01:17.039 --> 01:19.416
♪ I got pictures, got
candy, I'm a lovable man ♪

01:19.417 --> 01:21.426
♪ And I can take you
to the nearest star ♪

01:21.427 --> 01:24.105
♪ I'm your vehicle, baby ♪

01:24.106 --> 01:26.248
♪ I'll take you
anywhere you wanna go ♪

01:26.249 --> 01:28.092
♪ I'm your vehicle, woman ♪

01:28.093 --> 01:31.340
♪ By now I'm sure you know ♪

01:31.341 --> 01:32.713
- ♪ That I love ya ♪
- ♪ Love ya ♪

01:32.714 --> 01:34.121
- ♪ I need ya ♪
- ♪ Need ya ♪

01:34.122 --> 01:36.430
♪ I want you, got to have you, child ♪

01:36.431 --> 01:40.553
♪ Great God in heaven,
you know I love you... ♪

01:40.554 --> 01:42.562
- What's in your lunch?
- Pizza.

01:42.563 --> 01:44.002
From home or from a place?

01:44.003 --> 01:45.025
A place.

01:47.034 --> 01:50.200
♪ Well, if you wants
to be a movie star ♪

01:50.201 --> 01:52.763
♪ I'll get a ticket to Hollywood. ♪

01:55.449 --> 01:58.279
Griffin, you're three hours late.

01:58.280 --> 02:00.888
Stop trying to be a clock, you
ain't got the face for it.

02:00.889 --> 02:03.035
I've had enough of your nonsense.

02:03.036 --> 02:06.586
Here's Christoph Waltz to
fire you in a weird accent.

02:06.587 --> 02:09.785
Yer fi-yerd!

02:23.033 --> 02:24.423
It's a clich├й.

02:26.867 --> 02:28.325
You think you can fire me?

02:28.326 --> 02:31.190
I'm taking this keg as payback.

02:35.912 --> 02:38.142
Cinema is an event.

03:00.687 --> 03:03.869
- Where's my family?
- Dead. All of them.

03:21.686 --> 03:23.360
Oh, my God, where am I?

03:23.361 --> 03:25.671
- What happened?
- Ugh! Coma breath.

03:25.672 --> 03:27.647
Coma?! How long was I out?

03:27.648 --> 03:29.456
- What year is this?
- It's whatever year

03:29.457 --> 03:31.566
Quentin Tarantino used
to watch television.

03:31.567 --> 03:33.040
Well, can I go home?

03:33.041 --> 03:34.213
Well, you're not really ready,

03:34.214 --> 03:35.351
but if it's for revenge,

03:35.352 --> 03:36.825
you can stab me with this scalpel

03:36.826 --> 03:38.240
- and then run out.
- Thanks.

03:38.241 --> 03:40.937
Oh, that was unnecessary but cool.

03:40.938 --> 03:42.524
So awesome!

03:56.673 --> 03:58.282
Ah, so close.

04:02.467 --> 04:04.631
No, this is better.

04:08.815 --> 04:11.847
♪ ♪

04:17.373 --> 04:20.138
♪ Yeah. ♪

04:20.139 --> 04:22.380
Somebody order a wet-haired black guy

04:22.381 --> 04:24.491
to help with your
revenge and sometimes

04:24.492 --> 04:27.926
Speak louder than necessary?

04:31.610 --> 04:34.525
♪ ♪

04:38.637 --> 04:40.126
Angela?

04:40.127 --> 04:41.719
We got business.

04:48.240 --> 04:51.054
Sorry, that's my car alarm.
Cleveland, turn that off!

04:51.055 --> 04:52.528
I'm pressing the button.

04:52.529 --> 04:54.203
Y-You got to put the
keys in the ignition.

04:54.204 --> 04:55.475
I've been doing that, but...

04:55.476 --> 04:56.748
Oh, there we go.

04:56.750 --> 04:58.892
Tricia Takanawa 88s!

04:58.893 --> 05:01.926
♪ ♪

05:07.116 --> 05:09.442
Peter, I'm standing here because I am

05:09.443 --> 05:12.980
the only Asian recurring
character on the series.

05:59.019 --> 06:00.860
- ♪ Get on up ♪
- ♪ Get on up ♪

06:00.861 --> 06:03.070
- ♪ Get up ♪
- ♪ Get on up ♪

06:03.071 --> 06:04.712
- ♪ Get up ♪
- ♪ Get on up ♪

06:04.713 --> 06:07.326
- ♪ Get on up ♪
- ♪ Get on up ♪

06:07.327 --> 06:09.235
- ♪ Stay on the scene ♪
- ♪ Get on up ♪

06:09.236 --> 06:10.775
♪ Like a lovin' machine ♪

06:10.776 --> 06:12.183
♪ Get on up ♪

06:12.184 --> 06:13.757
- ♪ Get up ♪
- ♪ Get on up ♪

06:13.758 --> 06:16.269
- ♪ Taste ♪
- ♪ Get on up ♪

06:16.270 --> 06:18.129
- ♪ Of piano ♪
- ♪ Get on up. ♪

06:21.310 --> 06:23.671
Peter, you can tell I'm different

06:23.672 --> 06:25.818
because my weapon is different.

06:25.819 --> 06:27.490
Oh, well, then, maybe I won't be able

06:27.491 --> 06:28.714
to chop your head off.

06:30.287 --> 06:31.470
Oh, yep.

06:50.604 --> 06:53.635
♪ ♪

06:55.651 --> 06:58.164
Opera music makes violence classy.

07:06.836 --> 07:08.525
Of course.

07:08.526 --> 07:09.897
That!

07:09.898 --> 07:11.203
♪ What's new, pussycat? ♪

07:11.204 --> 07:13.113
♪ Whoa, whoa, whoa ♪

07:13.114 --> 07:15.842
♪ What's new, pussycat? Whoa. ♪

07:16.723 --> 07:18.582
Welcome back to our special episode,

07:18.583 --> 07:20.425
featuring famous directors' versions

07:20.426 --> 07:23.774
of the same Family Guy
story, "Peter Gets Fired."

07:23.775 --> 07:25.784
I'm still here in front
of the Hollywood Sign,

07:25.785 --> 07:27.828
but I've asked the cameraman
to adjust the shot

07:27.829 --> 07:29.589
so that you can only see "wood."

07:29.590 --> 07:31.244
I thought that would be hilarious.

07:31.245 --> 07:33.128
You know why? 'Cause of boners.

07:33.129 --> 07:36.269
Anyway, our next director
is Wes Anderson,

07:36.270 --> 07:38.614
a guy who makes you feel
like you ate a pot brownie

07:38.615 --> 07:40.531
and woke up in a greeting card.

07:59.880 --> 08:01.036
Mmm.

08:01.037 --> 08:02.777
Yum-yum-yum-yum-yum-yum-yum.

08:02.778 --> 08:06.159
On a March day, with a
temperature of 64 degrees,

08:06.160 --> 08:08.472
my father lost his position

08:08.473 --> 08:10.650
with the Pawtucket
Brothers Brewery Company,

08:10.651 --> 08:12.826
near our village in central Quahogia.

08:12.827 --> 08:16.611
Needless to say, it would
change our lives forever.

08:16.612 --> 08:18.688
What does it say? I
can't read spaghetti.

08:18.689 --> 08:20.699
You're relieved of your position.

08:20.700 --> 08:23.210
I see. And what's to
happen to my play?

08:23.211 --> 08:25.253
The opening is only days away.

08:25.254 --> 08:27.398
The play's off.

08:27.399 --> 08:29.272
With no discernible reaction,

08:29.273 --> 08:33.377
my father made his way home to
deliver the news to my mother.

08:49.791 --> 08:51.783
Let me tell you about my house.

08:51.784 --> 08:53.424
We lived in a New England cottage

08:53.425 --> 08:55.869
that was inside a vintage Army tent,

08:55.870 --> 08:58.281
that was inside a
decommissioned submarine,

08:58.282 --> 09:02.084
that was all inside an
old airplane hangar.

09:04.830 --> 09:06.187
I've lost my position

09:06.188 --> 09:08.262
with the Pawtucket
Brothers Brewery Company.

09:08.263 --> 09:09.838
And the play is off.

09:11.257 --> 09:13.821
We have to inform the children.

09:16.254 --> 09:17.709
My brother Chris had spent his life

09:17.710 --> 09:19.484
conjoining his twin loves,

09:19.485 --> 09:21.493
medicine and escape artistry.

09:21.494 --> 09:23.168
Eureka.

09:23.169 --> 09:25.281
A possible cure.

09:33.905 --> 09:37.606
Do you want to do a Spider-Man kiss?

09:38.633 --> 09:41.459
Our dog Brian had been
making a name for himself

09:41.460 --> 09:43.289
on the pickleball court.

09:49.984 --> 09:52.765
And that's match for Gene Porterfield.

09:55.175 --> 09:57.420
Are those marking sole shoes?

09:58.794 --> 10:01.020
I'd like to officially
file a grievance.

10:01.021 --> 10:03.365
Brian had quietly become
the most successful

10:03.366 --> 10:05.728
grievance filer in league history.

10:07.400 --> 10:09.394
I'll be there right away.

10:09.395 --> 10:11.839
The exterior of our house
is a lighthouse now.

10:11.840 --> 10:13.179
Inside's the same.

10:13.180 --> 10:15.174
Okay, back to the story.

10:16.546 --> 10:18.270
I've summoned you all and arranged you

10:18.271 --> 10:20.313
in a perfectly symmetrical
form in front of me

10:20.314 --> 10:22.155
to tell you some important news.

10:22.156 --> 10:24.902
I've been relieved of my
position at the brewery.

10:24.903 --> 10:26.142
What of the play?

10:26.143 --> 10:28.488
The play is postponed, indefinitely.

10:28.489 --> 10:29.694
No, Mr. Griffin.

10:29.695 --> 10:31.166
You need to do this play.

10:31.167 --> 10:32.340
We'll help you.

10:32.341 --> 10:34.014
But I've lost access to the brewery.

10:34.015 --> 10:35.857
That's where the whole piece is set.

10:35.858 --> 10:37.698
Maybe it doesn't have to be.

10:37.699 --> 10:39.808
But that's where the
free tape and paper is.

10:39.809 --> 10:41.785
I'll buy you new tape and paper.

10:41.786 --> 10:43.895
The play is back on.

10:43.896 --> 10:46.575
On an overcast Thursday afternoon,

10:46.576 --> 10:48.686
my father presented his play,

10:48.687 --> 10:51.600
one of the most compelling
stories of the 1980s,

10:51.601 --> 10:53.696
Max Dugan Returns.

10:54.732 --> 10:57.195
Max, you've returned!

10:57.196 --> 10:58.485
I have.

11:02.554 --> 11:04.999
This took a lot of work.

11:10.443 --> 11:14.043
My father passed away in the
spring of his 43rd year,

11:14.044 --> 11:17.378
and was put to rest in
the family graveyard.

11:17.379 --> 11:20.507
He died chasing a Pok├йmon
across a busy street.

11:20.508 --> 11:22.536
♪ ♪

11:30.860 --> 11:32.518
Hey there. It's me again.

11:32.519 --> 11:34.393
Wouldn't it be great if
Wes Anderson's movies

11:34.395 --> 11:36.236
were actually that short?

11:36.237 --> 11:39.518
Anyway, the Hollywood Sign is
more historic than you think.

11:39.519 --> 11:42.232
On this very spot, 52 years ago,

11:42.233 --> 11:44.745
a piece of beef jerky was
planted in the ground

11:44.746 --> 11:46.454
and watered with Red Bull.

11:46.455 --> 11:48.697
A speedboat erupted from the soil,

11:48.698 --> 11:51.878
and in that speedboat...
was Michael Bay.

11:59.801 --> 12:01.813
♪ ♪

12:31.523 --> 12:33.850
This already doesn't make sense.

12:33.851 --> 12:37.117
♪ ♪

12:58.818 --> 13:00.172
You're fired, Griffin,

13:00.173 --> 13:02.121
for destroying company property.

13:02.122 --> 13:03.831
Tell it to my tongue.

13:16.342 --> 13:18.401
Mr. President, we have a situation.

13:18.402 --> 13:22.151
The Decepticons plan to destroy
the Seven Wonders of the World,

13:22.152 --> 13:24.329
starting with the Hagia Sophia.

13:24.330 --> 13:27.545
The what? Is that even one
of the Seven Wonders?

13:27.546 --> 13:30.626
The Decepticons have
only one weakness.

13:30.627 --> 13:32.370
They're allergic to beer.

13:32.371 --> 13:34.647
I don't like the taste either so much.

13:34.648 --> 13:36.924
That chest plate is where
they're most vulnerable.

13:36.925 --> 13:39.469
If we could find someone
strong enough to throw a keg

13:39.470 --> 13:42.083
with enough force, we
might have a shot.

13:45.267 --> 13:47.644
The only problem is,
there's not a man alive

13:47.645 --> 13:50.643
who can throw a keg with
that kind of force.

13:51.646 --> 13:53.873
There may be one.

13:53.874 --> 13:56.185
I wonder who it is.

13:56.186 --> 13:58.212
♪ ♪

14:00.188 --> 14:03.722
Our top story, stopping the
Decepticons with beer?

14:03.723 --> 14:05.196
According to our sources,

14:05.197 --> 14:08.076
the search is underway
for a man strong enough

14:08.077 --> 14:10.214
to throw a keg with enough force

14:10.215 --> 14:12.231
to save the Seven
Wonders of the World.

14:16.367 --> 14:18.426
What took you so long?

14:18.427 --> 14:20.672
There was a train and I
like to count the cars.

14:20.673 --> 14:21.675
It was a big one.

14:21.676 --> 14:22.882
Me, too. That is fun.

14:22.883 --> 14:24.623
But you're wasting
your time coming here.

14:24.624 --> 14:26.834
I don't throw kegs anymore.

14:29.666 --> 14:30.853
Who's this?

14:30.854 --> 14:32.830
What are you wearing?
That's my funeral shirt.

14:32.831 --> 14:35.107
Look, Peter, I didn't want
to ask you to do this

14:35.108 --> 14:37.420
because of that maverick
but awesome thing you did

14:37.421 --> 14:39.362
in the battle war of the past.

14:39.363 --> 14:41.807
Is this the stuff you didn't
want me to ask you about?

14:41.808 --> 14:43.482
I told you not to ask me about that.

14:43.483 --> 14:46.094
He went rogue and saved
everyone's lives,

14:46.095 --> 14:47.736
but he didn't do it by the book.

14:47.737 --> 14:49.578
Is that why he can't get an erection?

14:49.579 --> 14:51.253
Everyone stop talking about me!

14:51.254 --> 14:53.698
Listen, it's not me that's asking,

14:53.699 --> 14:55.172
it's America.

14:57.117 --> 15:00.129
Tell America my answer is "no."

15:00.130 --> 15:02.407
Now, if you'll excuse me, I
have to go change my mind

15:02.408 --> 15:04.081
in the shower.

15:04.082 --> 15:07.565
♪ Peter's country needs him ♪

15:07.566 --> 15:10.548
♪ But he just doesn't know ♪

15:10.549 --> 15:13.092
♪ He's scared he'll miss his shows ♪

15:13.093 --> 15:16.609
♪ And he's expecting a UPS package ♪

15:16.610 --> 15:19.056
♪ Who's gonna water his plants? ♪

15:19.057 --> 15:21.902
♪ He's got a lot of balls in the air ♪

15:21.903 --> 15:23.409
♪ That's for sure. ♪

15:26.208 --> 15:27.615
Hold on!

15:28.620 --> 15:29.941
Damn it, I'm in.

15:29.942 --> 15:32.488
But I do things my way,
and I pick my crew.

15:32.489 --> 15:35.201
Deal. Now let me sit
sideways on your motorcycle

15:35.202 --> 15:38.215
like a Vietnamese woman,
and let's get out of here.

15:50.157 --> 15:53.039
Still trying to put the
world back together, I see.

15:55.851 --> 15:57.241
Hello, Peter.

15:57.242 --> 15:58.481
We're not joining your team.

15:58.482 --> 15:59.854
I'm putting together a team.

15:59.855 --> 16:01.261
- We're in.
- Good.

16:01.262 --> 16:03.289
Let's shake hands like tough guys.

16:04.627 --> 16:06.988
Some of your sweat went in my mouth.

16:16.687 --> 16:18.445
Oh, hello, Peter.

16:18.446 --> 16:20.690
I was just out back
working in the garden.

16:20.691 --> 16:21.694
Oh, yeah?

16:21.695 --> 16:23.235
Trying to grow some balls?

16:23.236 --> 16:25.378
Okay, okay.

16:25.379 --> 16:26.718
Play nice, boys.

16:31.258 --> 16:34.254
Love the cookie-cutter house
you and Poindexter got here.

16:34.255 --> 16:36.432
Never pegged you for a burbs dweller.

16:36.433 --> 16:38.108
Peter, you used to live here.

16:38.109 --> 16:39.346
That was a long time ago.

16:39.347 --> 16:40.887
It was two months ago.

16:40.888 --> 16:42.193
Two months is a long time

16:42.194 --> 16:44.974
when you don't sleep and
only eat ground beef.

16:44.975 --> 16:46.749
Did you tell Chris about my mission?

16:46.750 --> 16:48.826
I thought you should.

16:48.827 --> 16:50.199
This is my favorite

16:50.200 --> 16:52.175
out of all the Seven
Wonders of the World.

16:52.176 --> 16:54.286
The Hagia Sophia.

16:54.287 --> 16:57.534
It's like God made a
basilica for himself.

16:57.535 --> 16:59.745
Dad, nothing bad will ever happen

16:59.746 --> 17:01.989
to the Hagia Sophia, right?

17:01.990 --> 17:03.885
Not on my watch.

17:07.033 --> 17:09.026
The Decepticons' second target

17:09.027 --> 17:10.030
has been announced.

17:10.031 --> 17:11.605
It's Machu Picchu.

17:12.810 --> 17:14.085
City in the clouds.

17:14.886 --> 17:16.545
Inca Empire.

17:20.195 --> 17:23.326
When did our kids get so
obsessed with the Seven Wonders?

17:23.327 --> 17:25.772
They learned it from you.

17:26.781 --> 17:28.032
Got to go, babe.

17:28.033 --> 17:29.568
Pete.

17:30.296 --> 17:32.793
Save that basilica.

17:52.186 --> 17:55.116
According to the calculations
on my Microsoft Surface,

17:55.118 --> 17:57.528
they have advanced
cloaking technology.

17:57.529 --> 17:59.372
The Microsoft Surface confirms it.

17:59.372 --> 18:00.744
Microsoft Surface.

18:00.745 --> 18:04.279
My Samsung Gear S2 watch
says the same thing.

18:24.377 --> 18:28.849
We came from outer space
to step on church stuff.

18:28.850 --> 18:30.255
That does it.

18:30.256 --> 18:32.734
Let's have a fight with so many
quick shots and close-ups,

18:32.735 --> 18:34.408
you can't tell what's going on.

18:34.409 --> 18:37.087
♪ Up ♪

18:37.088 --> 18:41.835
♪ To break it back down ♪

18:41.837 --> 18:46.032
♪ We're building it up ♪

18:46.033 --> 18:47.772
♪ To burn it down ♪

18:47.773 --> 18:49.281
♪ We can't wait ♪

18:49.282 --> 18:52.274
♪ To burn it to the ground ♪

18:58.960 --> 19:02.539
♪ The colors conflict. ♪

19:26.412 --> 19:27.467
Peter, don't.

19:27.468 --> 19:29.075
It's suicide.

19:29.076 --> 19:32.323
Take care of my kids' bikes.

19:32.324 --> 19:33.849
They're expensive.

19:46.342 --> 19:48.588
♪ ♪

20:06.141 --> 20:07.328
Oh, my God!

20:07.330 --> 20:09.238
I can't believe Peter's gone.

20:09.239 --> 20:12.019
I never got to repeat to
him the line he said to me

20:12.020 --> 20:14.529
earlier in the film that
has taken on new meaning

20:14.530 --> 20:18.046
in the context of all
that has happened.

20:25.099 --> 20:28.799
Today is the day we honor
the late Peter Griffin,

20:28.800 --> 20:33.185
the hero who saved the Seven
Wonders of the World.

20:40.612 --> 20:42.723
Who's that ugly son of a bitch?

20:45.946 --> 20:47.623
Peter, you're alive.

20:47.625 --> 20:48.796
But-but how?

20:48.797 --> 20:51.040
You were blown into a million pieces.

20:51.041 --> 20:54.644
Luckily, I know a couple
of pretty good welders.

20:57.739 --> 20:59.921
Wait, they-they welded
you back together?

20:59.922 --> 21:02.128
A-And they knew you were
alive the whole time?

21:02.129 --> 21:05.730
You want to ask questions or you
want to do it in a cemetery?

21:10.637 --> 21:13.316
Is... is everything all right?

21:13.317 --> 21:14.822
Yeah, no, I-I think I'm just tired

21:14.823 --> 21:17.018
from all the flying back and forth.

21:17.019 --> 21:18.674
Maybe we just talk
here for a little bit,

21:18.675 --> 21:21.757
and then you can tell everyone
that I functioned as I should.

21:21.758 --> 21:23.734
Yeah, uh, okay.

21:23.735 --> 21:26.241
So, which director thing
